# The oracle image, pinned.
#
# One line per reference, tab-separated: <name> <image> <version> <what it answers>.
#
# This image is built here, so the tag is not a digest of the finished image.
# Two builds of one Containerfile are not two copies of one image. What is
# pinned instead is everything the build reads — the Debian base by digest,
# the openssl package by full apt version, Wycheproof by commit — and the
# run-time check is the guarantee. oracle_env.check_pin() therefore runs in
# both modes.
#
# The version field is what the reference must say. For openssl that is the
# library version, not the Debian revision: a disagreement with NIST's
# SHA-256("abc") is about OpenSSL 3.5.7. For Wycheproof the version is the
# commit, because the vectors are the data. containers/CORPUS hashes one file
# from that commit so a checkout of the right name with the wrong bytes fails
# `make check-oracle`.
#
# Building it:
#   make oracle-build

openssl	localhost/ghoti-security-oracle-openssl:3.5.7	OpenSSL 3.5.7	SHA-256 of a published input, and the openssl CLI for later known-answer differentials
wycheproof	localhost/ghoti-security-oracle-openssl:3.5.7	3fa63dd0344abb611f1fb1d77e119938603ea230	Negative test vectors at this commit; aes_gcm_test.json is hashed in CORPUS
